# 26. Test Matrix

Do more than five integration tests.

### Front Door

```text
policy question
normal conversation
direct cancellation
direct return
action + order ID
action without order ID
ambiguous action
human support
```

### Cancellation

```text
valid order
invalid order
order belonging to another customer
already cancelled
item selection
cancel confirmation
reject confirmation
```

### Return

```text
eligible order
outside return window
already returned
partial item return
return all
```

### Intent Switching

```text
cancel → return
return → cancel
cancel → human
return → human
cancel → FAQ → cancel
return → FAQ → return
```

### False-Positive Protection

Especially test things such as:

```text
product names containing "return"
notes containing "cancel"
order IDs containing digit patterns
button labels containing natural-language text
```

Expected-input validation should win first.

### Ambiguity

```text
"do the other one"
"change it"
"nah"
"something else"
```

The graph must never perform a transactional mutation based on ambiguous classification.

### Execution Safety

```text
double-click confirmation
duplicate request
network retry
graph retry
stale order state
DB exception
```

Mutation should occur at most once.

